      "evidence": "Charnwood publishes the full designated street list, so no ward mapping is needed or appropriate. The statutory public notice states: \"This designation shall cover whole and entire areas / roads within the existing boundaries for the duration of the 5 years Licensing Scheme and any future boundary changes shall not in any way alter the areas covered under this designation.\" The council repeats this on the scheme pages, confirming the May 2023 ward boundary review did not change the designated area, which remains defined by the historic Loughborough Hastings and Loughborough Lemyngton ward boundaries. Streets were transcribed from the two official council spreadsheets (Selective licensing Hastings ward - List of streets.xlsx and Selective Licensing Lemyngton Ward - List of Streets.xlsx) linked from charnwood.gov.uk, which match the HTML road lists exactly; Derby Road is designated for odd numbers only."
